---
import PracticeAreaLayout from '../../layouts/PracticeAreaLayout.astro';
---

<PracticeAreaLayout
  title="General Civil Legal Help | Maine Volunteer Lawyers Project"
  description="VLP may assist with bankruptcy, end-of-life documents, probate, SSDI/SSI appeals, immigrant family preparedness, and other civil legal matters."
  heading="General Civil Matters"
  intro="Free legal assistance with bankruptcy, benefit appeals, end-of-life planning, probate, immigrant family preparedness, and other civil legal needs."
  ctaHeading="Ready to get help with your civil legal matter?"
  ctaText="Complete an online intake form to request assistance. VLP staff will review your submission and follow up with you."
>

  <div slot="body">

    <h2>About General Civil Matters</h2>
    <p>VLP may be able to assist with a range of civil legal matters, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Bankruptcy</li>
      <li>Immigrant family protection preparedness</li>
      <li>End-of-life documents (advance directives, powers of attorney, wills)</li>
      <li>Probate</li>
      <li>SSDI/SSI denial appeals</li>
      <li>Unemployment insurance denial appeals</li>
      <li>Other civil legal matters</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How VLP Can Help</h2>

    <div class="notice-box">
      <p>
        Services are free with income-based eligibility. To request an
        appointment, complete the online intake form. A VLP staff member will
        follow up within one to two weeks. If you have an upcoming court date
        or deadline, please note it in your submission.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3>Probate Matters</h3>
    <p>
      For probate cases involving the distribution of property after someone's
      death, please contact the probate court in the relevant county first.
      Most of the time, you do not need an attorney to start or contest the
      probate process. Court staff can provide form assistance. Additional
      information is available at
      <a href="https://www.maineprobate.net/welcome/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">maineprobate.net</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      After contacting the probate court, you may then request legal help
      from VLP if needed.
    </p>

    <h3>Social Security Disability Appeals</h3>
    <p>
      VLP can only help with SSDI or SSI cases at the Administrative Law
      Judge hearing stage  -  meaning you have already been denied at the
      Reconsideration stage on your current application. If your initial
      application was denied, you must first request reconsideration before
      contacting VLP for assistance.
    </p>

    <h2>Additional Resources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/legal-help/family-matters">Family Matters</a>  -  divorce, parental rights, child custody and support</li>
      <li><a href="/legal-help/workers-rights">Workers' Rights</a>  -  harassment, discrimination, unpaid wages</li>
      <li><a href="/legal-help/small-claims">Small Claims</a>  -  disputes under $10,000</li>
      <li><a href="/legal-help/protection-from-abuse">Protection From Abuse</a>  -  PFA orders and walk-in court clinics</li>
    </ul>

  </div>

  <div slot="sidebar">

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>Eligibility</h3>
      <ul class="sidebar-list">
        <li>Maine legal matter or Maine court</li>
        <li>Limited income (generally at or below 200% of federal poverty level)</li>
        <li>Civil legal matter (not a criminal charge)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>Case Types</h3>
      <ul class="sidebar-list">
        <li>Bankruptcy</li>
        <li>Immigrant family preparedness</li>
        <li>Advance directives, POAs, wills</li>
        <li>Probate</li>
        <li>SSDI/SSI appeals (ALJ stage)</li>
        <li>Unemployment insurance appeals</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>Probate Resources</h3>
      <p>Contact your county probate court first  -  court staff can assist without an attorney in most cases.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.maineprobate.net/welcome/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">maineprobate.net →</a></p>
    </div>

  </div>

</PracticeAreaLayout>
